@buyaa-n I'm not sure I follow.

`optionalAttributeTypeFilter.IsSealed` is accessed inside a try-catch and is "optional" in the sense that it is just used as an optimization so we get the exception it's not a problem.

In contrast, if we sometimes can't check whether we're a generic type definition, then what do we do if the user passes an open generic type?
